cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "deadlinerisk: measured understatement of the mean-plus-margin deadline rule"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/deadlinerisk"
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
abstract: >-
  Measures the factor by which the mean-plus-margin sizing rule understates the
  counted deadline-miss rate of a periodic hard-real-time loop under named
  co-resident contention, with a moving-block bootstrap interval that accounts
  for serial dependence between consecutive deadlines. Includes a generalised
  Pareto peaks-over-threshold comparison with a declared threshold-stability
  diagnostic, a classical speed-scaling predictor, and a learned
  contention-aware predictor scored on held-out workload mixes and held-out
  time. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not certified, and not approved
  for operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - hard-real-time
  - deadline-miss
  - extreme-value-theory
  - moving-block-bootstrap
  - jetson-orin-nano
